  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financial and In-kind Assistance</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Titre II Programme d&apos;Urgence.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Titre II Programme d&apos;Urgence.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Financement pour fournir une aide alimentaire d&apos;urgence et des services de nutrition aux populations touch&#xe9;es par les conflits et les crises.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Programme d&apos;urgence Titre II &#xe0; travers un partenaire de l&apos;Agence am&#xe9;ricaine pour le d&#xe9;veloppement international.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this award is to provide a contribution of in-kind ready-to-use therapeutic food (RUTF) and financial support to treat 24,480 children under five years of age affected by severe acute malnutrition (SAM) for nutrition activities. This award contains a cash component and an in-kind component. USAID funds under the award will only be used for the approved itsh and section 202(E) funding level of $741,660. Of this, $328,600 will be provided in itsh and $413,060 will be provided in section 202(E) resources. USAIDs in-kind contribution of 340 mt of RUTF is valued at $1,150,900 (including $1,074,400 in commodity value, and $183,940 for ocean freight).</narrative>
  </description>
